abstract: "For kinetic (underdamped) Langevin samplers of a Gaussian target with matched target-preserving rotations, every square-integrable position observable has a long-run variance that never increases with rotation strength if and only if the friction is at least sqrt(2), a global form of a conjecture of Duncan, Nuesken and Pavliotis (2017). Also: the exact domain of the second-derivative statement; a below-threshold comparison (even observables always improve, finitely many odd degrees can be hurt, one finite rotation strength improves every observable); sharp large-rotation rates; the matrix criterion Gamma^3 - Gamma K - K Gamma >= 0 with least safe friction (2K)^(1/2); and observation schedules that do or do not preserve the ordering. Exact stationary Gaussian dynamics only; no claim about discretised integrators or cost. Unrefereed candidate; internal AI-assisted review only. Text CC0-1.0; code MIT."
